window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>MALDITA</b></p> <p>Spanish, feminine noun, meaning cursed or damned</p> <p>No matter how far you try to run away, some curses can never be escaped.</p> <p>Ten years ago when James had an affair with Cecilia, his high school Spanish teacher, he thought he would never see her again after she abruptly left town. But after a random conversation at the bar ignites his curiosity he decides to reach out again through email. Cecilia answers, wanting to meet up again and sets in motion a horrific series of events that will leave them both forever changed.</p> <p>Tlahuelpuchi, the legendary blood-sucking anthropomorphic witches prominent in Tlaxcala, dark shamanic magic and Mesoamerican gods come into play as an apocalyptic exodus takes place deep in the Mexican desert.</p>"; 
